From 162fb636d7758ff33ac6720ab9ed56abc8943e98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 20:06:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] compat: add the Qt4 compatibility layer

Two new pieces,both built on every Qt version so that there is a single
code path to test:

src/functorslot.{h,cpp}
    Qt4 can not connect a signal to a lambda or to a pointer to member
    function.  connectFunctor*() connects a SIGNAL() string to any
    callable through a small QObject carrying it as a real slot,parented
    to the context object so lifetime semantics match the Qt5 context
    object overload of QObject::connect().

src/qt4compat.{h,cpp}
    Drop in replacements for the classes SiriKali uses that Qt4 does not
    ship: QJson*(forwarded to the QJson4 library),QStandardPaths,
    QLockFile and QStorageInfo.  QStandardPaths resolves to the same
    paths Qt5 does so a Qt4 and a Qt5 build share their configuration,
    and QStorageInfo is a real implementation(getmntinfo on the BSDs and
    macOS,/proc/self/mounts on linux) rather than the empty stub
    compatibility.hpp used to carry.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
